{"book":24,"chapter":38,"context":{"chapter":38,"title":"Rescued From the Mud","summary":"Officials lower Jeremiah into a muddy cistern to die, but Ebed-melech, a Cushite official, persuades the king and hauls him out with ropes and rags. In another secret meeting Zedekiah hears that surrender means life, but he is too afraid to act.","background":"Cisterns were bell-shaped pits cut into rock to store rainwater; late in the siege this one held only mud (v. 6). Ebed-melech, meaning 'servant of the king,' came from Cush, south of Egypt. Clay seal impressions found in Jerusalem bear the names 'Gedalyahu son of Pashhur' and 'Yehukal son of Shelemyahu,' matching officials named in verse 1.","customs":[{"term":"Old cast clouts and rotten rags","verses":"38:11-12","note":"Worn-out cloth to pad Jeremiah's armpits so the ropes would not cut him: a small act of care in a desperate rescue."}],"watchFor":["'The king is not he that can do any thing against you' (v. 5): a weak king.","Ebed-melech's courage (vv. 7–10), rewarded in 39:15-18.","The image of sinking in the mire is turned on the king (v. 22)."],"connections":["Jeremiah 39:15-18","Psalms 40:2","Psalms 69:2","Genesis 37:24"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיִּשְׁמַע","vaiyishma'","H8085","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he heard"],["שְׁפַטְיָה","shefatyah","H8203","HNpm","Shephatiah"],["בֶן","ven-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["מַתָּן","matan","H4977","HNpm","Mattan"],["וּגְדַלְיָהוּ","ugedalyahu","H1436","HC/Npm","and Gedaliah"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["פַּשְׁחוּר","pashchur","H6583","HNpm","Pashhur"],["וְיוּכַל","veyukhal","H3116","HC/Npm","and Jucal"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["שֶׁלֶמְיָהוּ","shelemyahu","H8018","HNpm","Shelemiah"],["וּפַשְׁחוּר","ufashchur","H6583","HC/Npm","and Pashhur"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["מַלְכִּיָּה","malkiyah","H4441","HNpm","Malkijah"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַדְּבָרִים","hadevarim","H1697","HTd/Ncmpa","the words"],["א